    "problem_statement": "[Bug]: `ChunkedInsert` context manager returns None instead of self\n\n### Bug summary\n\nWhen using the `ChunkedInsert` context manager with a `with` statement, it returns `None` instead of the chunker object itself, making it impossible to use the context manager properly.\n\n### Code for reproduction\n\n```python\nfrom dataset import chunked\n\n# Create a table first\nimport dataset\ndb = dataset.connect('sqlite:///:memory:')\ntable = db.create_table('test')\n\n# Try to use ChunkedInsert as a context manager\nwith chunked.ChunkedInsert(table) as chunk_tbl:\n    # This will fail because chunk_tbl is None, not a chunker object\n    chunk_tbl.insert({'name': 'John', 'age': 30})\n```\n\n### Actual outcome\n\n```\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<stdin>\", line 3, in <module>\nAttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'insert'\n```\n\nThe context manager returns `None` instead of the chunker object, so trying to call `insert()` on it raises an AttributeError.\n\n### Expected outcome\n\nThe context manager should return the chunker object itself, allowing you to call methods like `insert()` on it:\n\n```python\nwith chunked.ChunkedInsert(table) as chunk_tbl:\n    # This should work\n    chunk_tbl.insert({'name': 'John', 'age': 30})\n```\n\n### Additional information\n\nThis affects all chunked operations that use the context manager pattern.\n\n### Version information\n\ndataset version: latest"
  },
